# Production build config for the IntelAI frontend.
#
# Left blank on purpose: frontend/src/api.js falls back to a same-origin relative
# base ("/api/v1") when VITE_API_BASE_URL is unset, which is correct for the
# self-hosting story in the Dockerfile (FastAPI serves frontend/dist/ itself — see
# src/api/server.py's "/" route — so frontend and backend share an origin, no base
# URL needed). frontend/src/pages/ApiDocs.tsx uses the same fallback order so its
# copy-paste examples always match wherever it's actually being served from.
#
# If you deploy the frontend and backend SEPARATELY (e.g. Vercel frontend + a
# different backend host), set VITE_API_BASE_URL in your hosting platform's own
# environment-variable configuration (e.g. the Vercel project dashboard) at deploy
# time — don't hardcode a real URL into this file; it's a committed template shared
# by every clone of this repo. VITE_API_URL / REACT_APP_API_URL are left blank for
# the same reason (REACT_APP_API_URL is only read by an unused legacy hook).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
VITE_API_URL=
REACT_APP_API_URL=
